bpftune (0.4.39) UNRELEASED; urgency=medium

  * Diagnostic: emit snd_cwnd and packets_out on each vote.

    The live trace on the heavy host showed the kernel's app_limited
    flag set on ~96% of sockets.  If that holds, most votes measure
    the app's supplied rate rather than the path's capacity, and the
    per-algorithm bucket EMAs would converge on the app's rate
    instead of the algorithm's capability.  The observed 34-65%
    spread between best and worst algorithm on busy buckets
    (versus the 200%+ a genuine difference would show) is
    consistent with this dilution, but is not by itself enough to
    prove it.

    Fix can't be designed until the size of the problem is known,
    and the app_limited flag is not exposed to BPF.  packets_out vs
    snd_cwnd is the proxy: when packets_out << snd_cwnd the app has
    not filled the window the algorithm permits.  Both fields are
    on bpf_tcp_sock and already in scope at the vote site.

    A second printk line joins by cookie to the existing met line.
    Split because the met line is already at the 12-argument printk
    limit.  Doubles the met log volume for the duration of the
    diagnostic.

    No metric logic change.  No struct change.  No state file change.

 -- Christophe Deppe <cddeppe@users.noreply.github.com>  Wed, 16 Sep 2026 17:00:00 +0200

bpftune (0.4.38) UNRELEASED; urgency=medium

  * Fix the 0.4.37 flat-gate: relax the required sample count
    from 3 to 2.

    0.4.37 introduced a flat-socket gate on the moderate swap tier
    that required all three of {last_metric, hist_1, hist_2} to be
    populated before it could classify a socket.  Root cause of the
    failure: SWAP_BAD_FIRST=2 fires the first moderate swap after
    two consecutive bad votes.  On a fresh socket -- or one whose
    history was zeroed by a prior swap -- hist_2 is still 0 at the
    moment the swap fires.  The gate therefore never fired on the
    exact population it was designed to suppress: 0.4.37 moderate
    swap rate was unchanged from 0.4.36 (7 fires in 3h vs pre-gate
    baseline of ~47/day).

    Validation from the 09-14 + 09-15 pre-gate logs, binning swaps
    by number of samples on the current algorithm:

        2sample-flat      n=85    win ~10%   <- gate now catches
        2sample-nonflat   n=17    win ~48%   <- max/min check excludes
        1sample           n=218   win ~38%   <- insufficient, falls
                                              through (unchanged)
        3sample           n=57    win mixed  <- unchanged

    Data confirms 2sample-flat is the same population as 3sample-
    flat by win rate (~10% vs ~8%), well below the tier target.
    2sample-nonflat stays at 45-50% and is not gated.

  * hist_1/hist_2 remain in struct conn_state; swap-path resets
    unchanged.  No state-format change: STATE_VERSION stays at 12,
    no state file delete on deploy.

 -- Christophe Deppe <cddeppe@users.noreply.github.com>  Tue, 15 Sep 2026 22:00:00 +0200

bpftune (0.4.37) UNRELEASED; urgency=medium

  * Flat-socket gate on the moderate swap tier.
    Over 340 swaps in the 09-14 + 09-15 met logs, binning by the
    shape of the socket's own last three metric samples shows flat
    sockets win only 7.9% (90.6% null, 1.6% loss) -- inside the
    metric's own noise band.  Rising runs 57.9% win, oscillating
    16.7%, falling 27.3%.  The moderate tier selects for flat:
    78.5% of its fires are flat sockets vs 21.9% in desperate.  A
    socket that is deteriorating climbs through 1.5x-2.0x fast and
    trips the desperate bar at 2.0x; a flat socket sits at a fixed
    ratio and eventually trips moderate on the 2-bad-check rule.
  * Add hist_1/hist_2 to struct conn_state; the vote path shifts
    the previous two samples and the swap path resets them.  Gate
    the moderate-tier swap on max/min of the three >= 1.10.
  * Desperate and insufficient-history sockets are untouched:
    desperate fires on the 2x rule regardless of shape, and a
    socket with fewer than three samples has not been judged yet
    (42.4% win rate, the largest source of real wins besides
    rising).
  * Sk_storage only (conn_state); the persisted state file layout
    is unchanged, STATE_VERSION stays at 12, no state file delete
    needed on deploy.

