bpftune (0.4.36) UNRELEASED; urgency=medium

  * Userspace re-anchor for the tcp_conn_tuner tracker.
    The BPF vote path maintains best_i/best_v incrementally and the
    ESTABLISHED-time rescan refreshes it on new connections, but
    between those events a non-leader metric can drift to a lower
    value without being promoted.  Observed on the home bucket:
    best_i pointed at htcp at 1.79M while dctcp at 608K had n=5 and
    was never promoted, so swaps targeted a non-leader.
  * Add a daemon worker thread that every 30s walks remote_host_map,
    finds the trusted minimum (metric_count >= MIN_LEADER_TRUST) and
    second-best, and writes best_i/best_v/second_i/second_v back
    via bpf_map_update_elem.  Read-modify-write preserves the
    reference-fix fields (rate_high_streak etc.) and every other
    field in the struct.
  * No BPF change, no state version change.  The swap path keeps
    reading the same tracker fields it reads today.

