bpftune (0.4.35) UNRELEASED; urgency=medium

  * Collapse the split settle window into a single constant.
    0.4.33 introduced T_SETTLE_NORMAL_NS (60s) / T_SETTLE_DESPERATE_NS
    (10s), chosen by whether the socket was desperate or had hit
    persist_bad >= 2.  In practice the 60s branch was unreachable:
    any moderate swap requires SWAP_BAD_FIRST/LATER = 2 consecutive
    above-margin checks, which is exactly the condition that sets
    persist_bad >= 2.  So every swap took the 10s branch, and the
    60s branch was dead code.
  * Remove the persist_bad counter, PERSIST_BAD_THRESHOLD and both
    split constants.  The socket-level truth is: after 2 consecutive
    bad checks we already know the socket is stuck; a full-minute
    wait between retries was never useful.
  * conn_state no longer carries persist_bad.  STATE_VERSION
    11 -> 12.  State file MUST be deleted on deploy.

 -- Christophe Deppe <cddeppe@users.noreply.github.com>  Tue, 15 Sep 2026 17:00:00 +0200

bpftune (0.4.34) UNRELEASED; urgency=medium

  * Moderate-tier margin raised from 1.25x to 1.50x.
    Observed: on buckets where top algorithms are within ~10%
    of each other (TIGHT x1.0/x1.1), the 1.25x-1.50x band is
    inside the metric's noise.  Swaps fired in that band landed
    below a coin flip (12 IMP / 15 WRS over one day).  Raising
    the floor to 1.50x keeps the tier for meaningful moderate
    cases (1.50-2.00x) and drops the noise band.
  * Post-freeze desperate tier now judges against the socket's
    own best_seen_metric, not the bucket leader.  Observed: a
    frozen socket (cookie 2927) cycled eight more times through
    bic/veno/illinois/highspeed/htcp while every algorithm
    produced 12-14M -- the socket was at its path ceiling, not
    algorithm-limited.  The bucket-relative 2x test kept firing
    because the bucket best_v was 5.6M (other sockets ran
    faster on the same path).  Now: a frozen socket only gets a
    post-freeze desperate swap if last_metric >= best_seen * 2.
    Pre-freeze behavior unchanged.
  * No struct changes.  STATE_VERSION unchanged.

 -- Christophe Deppe <cddeppe@users.noreply.github.com>  Tue, 15 Sep 2026 16:00:00 +0200

