bpftune (0.4.30) UNRELEASED; urgency=medium

  * Two-tier swap trigger.
    - Desperate tier: socket_metric >= best_v * 2.00 fires
      immediately, regardless of bad_checkpoints.  Very bad
      sockets do not wait.
    - Normal tier: socket_metric >= best_v * 1.25 requires
      SWAP_BAD_FIRST (2, changed from 1) consecutive bad
      checkpoints on the first swap; SWAP_BAD_LATER (2) on
      subsequent swaps.
    Observed churn: on a bucket where the top-8 algorithms were
    within 20% of each other, sockets on 1.25-1.5x readings
    swapped back and forth as the leader moved -- 137 swaps/day
    on the heavy host, with a dip in user experience on YouTube
    Shorts.  The two-tier split targets that: sockets in the
    churn band wait for confirmation, sockets genuinely stuck
    fire immediately.
  * Swap printk extended with bc= (bad_checkpoints at fire),
    ac= (source algorithm bucket vote count), and d= (1 = fired
    via desperate tier, 0 = normal tier).  So we can measure
    which tier produced which outcome over the next day.
  * No STATE_VERSION bump (no struct field changes).

 -- Christophe Deppe <cddeppe@users.noreply.github.com>  Mon, 14 Sep 2026 20:00:00 +0200

bpftune (0.4.29) UNRELEASED; urgency=medium

  * Add a time-based supplementary vote: every 60 seconds, if the
    socket has advanced by >= 1000 segments since the last time
    check, the vote + swap decision runs even if no segment
    checkpoint was reached.  Fixes the case where a long-lived
    socket (past the 1M rung, where nextp is ~0) can go many
    minutes without re-evaluation while the path degrades.
  * Raise the post-swap settle window from 5s to 60s, matching
    the time-check cadence.  This is the rate limiter now.
  * Remove SWAP_MAX.  No total cap per socket; a long socket can
    swap as often as needed, at most once per settle window.
  * Swap decision: when the socket is on best_i and best_i's
    metric is worse than second_i's by 1.25x for this socket,
    swap to second_i.  Handles the case where the leader is
    performing badly for a particular socket but the bucket's
    EMA hasn't caught up yet.  Because second_v >= best_v, the
    1.25x bar is naturally higher than the normal case, so this
    fires rarely.
  * STATE_VERSION 7 -> 8 (struct conn_state gained two fields).
    State file MUST be deleted on deploy.

