bpftune (0.4.28) UNRELEASED; urgency=medium

  * Add loss rate as a metric axis.  metric is now
    rtt_term + rate_term + loss_term, where loss_term =
    min(retrans/segs_out, LOSS_CAP_BP) / LOSS_CAP_BP * LOSS_SCALE
    with LOSS_CAP_BP=200 (2.00%).  The met log line gains a loss=
    field so the distribution can be observed live.
  * Remove the hardcoded forced-BBR rescue in RETRANS_CB.  It
    predated the per-destination metric and bypassed it: any
    socket above ~1.56% loss was switched to BBR and its RTT_CB
    flag cleared, so lossy sockets could never vote for any other
    algorithm.  With loss now in the metric, the tuner can learn
    per-path which algorithm handles loss best; the forced BBR
    shortcut is no longer needed.  The TCP_THIN_LINEAR_TIMEOUTS
    opt-in for lossy sockets is kept.
  * STATE_VERSION 6 -> 7 (metric formula changed; old bucket
    values are not comparable).  State file MUST be deleted on
    deploy.

