bpftune (0.4.23) UNRELEASED; urgency=medium

  * Fix cold-start coverage to count selections, not votes.  The 0.4.22
    coverage loop gated on per-algorithm metric_count, which only
    increments when a socket actually votes (at 10K segments, or at
    close above 100 segments).  Sockets that never vote did not advance
    the coverage pointer, so the same algorithm was assigned to every
    new connection until one of its sockets happened to vote.  Observed
    on the heavy host minutes after 0.4.22 deploy: cubic 149, htcp 99,
    bbr 84, and indices 6-15 at zero.
  * Add __u64 selection_count to struct remote_host.  Increment on
    every ESTABLISHED; force-pick algorithm (selection_count & 15)
    while selection_count < 32.  Now the first 32 connections to a
    bucket get exactly two of each algorithm, regardless of whether
    any socket votes.  STATE_VERSION 3 -> 4.

 -- Christophe Deppe <cddeppe@users.noreply.github.com>  Sun, 13 Sep 2026 18:30:00 +0200

bpftune (0.4.22) UNRELEASED; urgency=medium

  * Margin-gated exploitation.  Track leader and second-place metric in
    one pass (no extra iterations); if the leader is not >=25% ahead of
    second, boost exploration from 1/20 to 1/4 until a clear winner
    emerges.  Prevents the tuner from committing to a leader whose
    early samples look better than they are.
  * Coverage gate lowered from 5 back to 2.  Coverage=5 required 80
    sockets per bucket before exploit could start, which most
    destinations never reach.  Coverage=2 is enough to establish a
    first-pass distribution; the margin gate then decides whether the
    evidence supports committing.
  * Remove tie-break machinery from the selection path.  With
    cold-start coverage guaranteeing every algorithm has real samples,
    the multi-candidate random selection and its 16-case switch are
    dead weight; on a program already at the 1,000,000-instruction
    verifier limit, dropping them is what makes room for the margin
    gate.  Ties now resolve by lowest index.

 -- Christophe Deppe <cddeppe@users.noreply.github.com>  Sun, 13 Sep 2026 17:30:00 +0200

bpftune (0.4.21) UNRELEASED; urgency=medium

  * metric_value: replace slow-learning rolling update with count-based
    incremental mean (divisor min(count+1, METRIC_AVG_CAP=32)). Previous
    update applied a fixed 25% step per observation, giving the metric an
    effective memory of ~4 samples regardless of sample count. Home-bucket
    leader churn observed 2026-09-13 (bbr 5.8M -> 7.59M over 5 votes) was
    this step size, not path drift.
  * Skip addresses that do not benefit from CC tuning: 127.0.0.0/8,
    169.254.0.0/16, ::1, fe80::/10.
  * Add remote_port to midsamp and closport printks, so incoming 443
    connections can be paired reliably.
  * Cold-start coverage: on a fresh bucket, force-sample the
    least-sampled algorithm until every algorithm has >= 2 votes,
    then fall back to normal epsilon-greedy.  Without this, a lucky
    first sample locks the leader in and the exploration rate (5%/16
    per non-leader) is too thin to recover.  Bounded cost: at most 32
    sockets, then zero overhead.
  * Raise cold-start coverage from 2 to 5 votes per algorithm before
    exiting the round-robin phase, so the tuner does not begin
    exploiting a leader whose early samples may have been lucky.
    Bounded cost: 80 sockets per fresh bucket, then zero overhead.
  * Remove dead per-algorithm min_rtt / max_rate_delivered fields from
    struct tcp_conn_metric. Displayed but never read by the metric.
    STATE_VERSION 2 -> 3.

  DEPLOY: the state file MUST be deleted between stop and start.
  Metric semantics changed (new averaging) and the struct changed
  (STATE_VERSION 3). Preserving state would poison the new average.

 -- Christophe Deppe <cddeppe@users.noreply.github.com>  Sun, 13 Sep 2026 23:00:00 +0200

